  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "p-B11 fusion gain Q≥1 is achievable via non-thermal acceleration (block ignition for Marvel, avalanche fast ignition for HB11), bypassing the ~10–15× higher temperature requirement vs D-T",
      "DPSSL laser systems can scale to ~10% wall-plug efficiency at petawatt-class peak power and 10 Hz continuous operation with kilojoule-per-pulse energies",
      "Laser diode costs can fall ~30–130× from current $0.3–$1.3/W to the $0.01/W IFE viability target, which requires ~1000× production volume increase tied to IFE deployment",
      "Diode pump reliability can reach 3–20 Gshots over plant lifetime, vs ~1–2 Gshots demonstrated today",
      "Marvel's hybrid magnetic + electrostatic + steam direct energy conversion can reach ~70% efficiency for pulsed alpha-particle capture (no built or demonstrated analogue)",
      "Nanostructured silicon targets can be manufactured at <$0.03/target with 864,000/day throughput at 10 Hz via standard semiconductor lithography",
      "Plant availability of ~75% is achievable for a 10 Hz pulsed laser IFE plant with no operational analogue"
    ],
